    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="0853" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">093.612/52: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-27">March 27,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received March 28—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1067. Moscow papers for March 25 announce the award of the Order of Suvorov First
                    Class to General Marshall “for distinguished military activity and services in
                    the direction of the American Armed Forces in the struggle against the common
                    enemy of the Soviet Union and the United States of America, Hitlerite
                        Germany”.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d775-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d775-f1" n="4" xml:id="d775-f1-content">
                <p>Moscow newspapers for June 7 reported the presentation ceremony at the Soviet
                    Embassy in Washington on June 5.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
